% The gchord and drum strings start on the bar line that follows a pickup
% (GitHub issue #96).  After a pickup shorter than the first element of a
% string, abc2midi played the second element of the first full bar early,
% and the other elements of this bar with the same shift.
% - Tune 1: 6/8 with a pickup of one eighth, and strings of four elements
%   of a dotted eighth.
% - Tune 2: 4/4 with a pickup of one quarter, a gchord string of two
%   elements of a half note and a drum string of one element of a whole
%   note, which abc2midi played twice at each bar line.
X:1
T:Pickup shorter than a gchord unit in 6/8
C:abc2midi test
M:6/8
L:1/8
Q:3/8=60
%%MIDI gchord bhcb
%%MIDI drum dddd 35 38 42 38
K:C
%%MIDI drumon
"C"G|"C"c6|"G"B6|"C"c6|]

X:2
T:Pickup shorter than a gchord unit in 4/4
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=120
%%MIDI gchord fc
%%MIDI drum d 35
K:C
%%MIDI drumon
"C"G2|"C"c8|"G"B8|"C"c8|]
